      "documentConcept": "Tremor, gait, freezing and postural instability management",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:d3e1b1a9a1a2278548cf6fa2bc5d27a952b02b4dba994fcb1daf98faab819eac",
      "text": "Tremor and axial disability require symptom-specific assessment. Levodopa is the principal drug approach for troublesome tremor, and apparent resistance can reflect inadequate treatment delivery. Persistent disabling tremor can warrant specialist invasive-treatment assessment. Freezing must be assessed in relation to medication state: OFF, pseudo-ON and true ON freezing need different interpretations. Reducing OFF time may help OFF freezing, but persistent gait and balance problems also require Parkinson-specific physiotherapy. Rivastigmine gait findings are promising phase 2 evidence rather than established freezing treatment. Methylphenidate evidence is inconsistent, with a negative randomized trial despite permissive consensus guidance.",
